course: dictionary
lesson: 15140
title: Scarp: a steep edge in the land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scarp is a steep slope or cliff. Picture a sudden step in the land, where the ground drops away quickly. «The walkers climbed up the scarp, pulling on rocks to reach the top.» Steep means the ground rises or falls at a sharp angle, so climbing it is hard work.
explain: Scarps often form a long line, like a wall along the edge of a hill. «From the valley, we could see a long grey scarp running for miles along the moor.» The word long is the clue: a scarp is a whole edge of steep ground, not one small step.
explain: You can check your meaning by swapping in a word you know. «The walkers climbed up the steep slope to reach the top.» It still makes sense, so steep slope is a good match for scarp. In geography, the steep side of a ridge is a scarp, and the gentle side is the dip slope.
fact: A scarp is a steep slope or cliff.
fact: Another word for a scarp in geography is an escarpment.
fact: Scarps can form when land is worn away, or when the ground moves along a crack called a fault.
fact: «Scarp» can also mean the inner steep wall of a ditch around a castle, which made attackers find it hard to climb in.
fact: Earthquakes can make fault scarps, when the ground suddenly shifts and leaves a steep step.
exercise: «The walkers climbed up the steep scarp to reach the top.» What is a scarp? | *A steep slope or cliff | A deep, dark cave | A flat field for sheep | A small river that runs to the sea
exercise: «The castle's ditch had a steep scarp on the inside, so attackers could not climb up easily.» In a castle, where is the scarp? | The roof of the tallest tower | The lawn in the courtyard | *The inner steep wall of a ditch | The gate where visitors come in
exercise: «From the valley, we could see a long scarp of grey rock.» What does the word long tell you about the scarp? | It is a small pool of water | *It is a long line of steep ground | It is a short path for bikes | It is a soft, flat meadow
test: Ella says a scarp is a flat, grassy field. Is she right? | *No, a scarp is steep, not flat | Yes, because it is a field for cows | Yes, but only in summer | Yes, because it is grassy
test: «The earthquake left a new scarp across the hills.» What made the new scarp? | A rainbow after the rain | A cake left in the oven | *Ground moving along a fault | A heavy snowball fight
exam: Which sentence uses the word scarp correctly? | The scarp was a sweet, soft cake for the picnic | *The climbers stopped at the top of the scarp, where the ground dropped steeply away | The scarp was a loud noise in the night | We played a game of scarp on the beach
